Subject: [PATCH] main: daynight sidecar read in main() + sigaltstack + startup trace + UNBUFFERED DIAG markers
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (stacks on 0001-0014)

DIAGNOSTIC BUILD. The daynight minimal-write feature reads /etc/daynight.state in
main() (apply_daynight_sidecar, NOT in CFG::load -- moved there to keep CFG::load
byte-identical to the proven build). But the daemon still SIGSEGVs at startup inside
libuclibcshim BEFORE any of that code runs -- the buffered Logger hid which step
faults.

This build adds UNBUFFERED markers: a DIAG(x) macro that does a raw write(2, ...)
(direct syscall, no stdio/Logger buffering) at every early-startup step, plus one
at the crash-handler entry. The LAST "DIAG:" line on stderr before the segfault
pins the exact faulting statement:

  A  = entered main body (post bootstrap log)
  B  = instance lock acquired
  B2 = sigaltstack registered
  C  = signal handlers installed (sigaction done)
  D  = recover_stale_imp_state() returned
  D2 = about to call make_shared<CFG>()
  E  = make_shared<CFG>() returned (CFG::load done)
  F  = apply_daynight_sidecar() returned
  HANDLER entered = the crash handler ran (so a missing crash log = file-write issue,
                    not handler-never-runs)

So: last marker "C" -> crash in recover_stale_imp_state(); "D2" -> crash inside
CFG::load(); "E" -> crash in apply_daynight_sidecar(); etc. All of A..D are
PROVEN Jun-26 code, so if the crash lands there it confirms 0015's mere presence
(binary layout/codegen shift) trips a latent shim fault rather than any new logic.

Also keeps the sigaltstack/SA_ONSTACK crash-handler hardening. Allocation-free
sidecar read (raw open/read, C buffers, static literals).

Verified: git apply --check + patch -p1 both pass against f4b3228 + 0001-0014.

